WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:11.500
France is the only country that makes Americans look humble.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.129
The ego of the French is so colossal that
it doesn’t even fit within its own country’s borders.

00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:21.930
Which explains why France spent the nineteenth
century colonizing other countries...

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:24.230
Almost half of Africa was a French colony.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.750
And I bet you can guess the most widely spoken language in sub-Saharan Africa?

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.750
Exactly!

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:30.750
French!

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.480
But not only that!

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:39.220
You’ve all heard that Latin America is the
US’s backyard, right?

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.030
Well, we could say that Africa is France’s
backyard.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:48.940
For example, in 2011, France led every military
operation against Gaddafi.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:55.970
Two years later, Francois Hollande’s government
sent troops to defend the

00:00:55.970 --> 00:01:00.579
President of the Central African Republic
while, at the same time, French soldiers were

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:03.030
also fighting Islamic terrorists in Mali.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:08.290
Basically, the French army has been present
in virtually every African armed conflict.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:11.550
France even controls the currency that many
African countries use.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:17.000
In other words, even though African countries
gained independence from France decades ago,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.750
it still maintains a strong influence on their
governments.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:27.320
You can call it soft power, diplomacy or,
simply, colonialism 2.0.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.030
And I know what many of you may be thinking...

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:34.660
France must be getting rich off of its African
colonies!

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:35.660
Really?

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:42.760
Well, my dear friends, nothing could be further
from the truth.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:47.750
In the last 10 years, France's trade with
Africa has dropped from 10 to 4.7%

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:48.860
You heard that right!

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:54.990
Even though France dominates African politics,
its economy is an entirely different story.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:02:01.080
In fact, after centuries of colonialism and
neocolonialism, African countries have barely

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.080
evolved.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.090
Hardly any new companies have emerged due
to French investment.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:09.590
And, meanwhile, France is spending billions
of euros every year to maintain its share

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:14.239
of influence over the continent, even though,
ultimately, it barely gets any benefits.

00:02:14.239 --> 00:02:15.239
And...

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:20.900
I bet you can’t guess who’s reaping all
the benefits of collaborating with Africa?

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:21.900
Exactly!

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:28.730
We’re talking about…

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.610
Chinese companies and Africa need each other
like never before

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:37.310
For the last ten years, Chinese investment
has changed the skyline of almost all African

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:38.310
cities.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:43.200
Some countries like Ethiopia are becoming
industrial powers, especially in the textile

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.200
sector.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.750
Chinese companies aren’t only taking advantage
of the cheap labor, they have also found a

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.440
new market to sell their products to!

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:55.080
Chinese mobiles are sweeping across Africa
and more and more people are learning Confucius’s

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.080
language instead of Moliere's.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:00.480
In other words, while France sends soldiers,
China sends businessmen.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.240
And it looks like it’s working out pretty
well for them.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:08.550
So the question remains: Why has France failed
to capitalize on its influence in Africa?

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:13.510
And what can the new French president, Emmanuel
Macron, do to improve this situation?

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:21.040
Today we’re going to answer this question
but first, a bit of history.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.080
THE DISADVANTAGES OF PATERNALISM

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:27.320
Those who’ve been following VISUALPOLITIK
already know that after World War II, every

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:36.650
African country became independent from its
colonizers.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:40.540
But make no mistake, not every colonizer behaved
the same way!

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:45.340
For example, Spain had two colonies in Africa:
Sahara and Equatorial Guinea.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:49.099
When these two countries decided to become
independent, the Spanish government said “Ehm…

00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:50.099
Hey dude…

00:03:50.099 --> 00:03:51.260
Did we have colonies in Africa?

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.260
Really?

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.770
OK, well… ahm… well I guess if they want
to go, we should let them…

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:56.250
I mean… we already have enough problems
to deal with, don’t we?”

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.170
Something similar happened with Italy.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:03.430
They had invaded Ethiopia during Mussolini's
time and weren’t in a position to resist

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.520
decolonization much.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:10.170
However, France was very different.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.660
At that time, the French president was this
guy, CHARLES DE GAULLE.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.069
Charles de Gaulle was...

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:16.850
How can I define him?

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:22.639
Something like Donald Trump but with a brain.

00:04:22.639 --> 00:04:29.590
“France cannot be France without its greatness”
--Charles de Gaulle

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:35.960
On the one hand, de Gaulle had no choice but
to allow its African colonies to become independent.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.960
Maintaining colonies is very expensive and
France still had to rebuild itself.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:44.250
But, as you can imagine, a government with
so much ego wasn’t going to entirely give

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.250
up its old possessions.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:50.669
So France kept its army in all its former
colonies and, from the Elysee Palace, decided

00:04:50.669 --> 00:04:56.590
to “support” every one of the political
elites that had begun governing these new

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:58.590
African countries.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:06.740
For example, in 1964, the French army supported
a coup in Gabon.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:12.069
Since then, Gabon was governed by OMAR BONGO’s
dictatorship for more than 40 years.

00:05:12.069 --> 00:05:14.590
And who supplied all the weapons?

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:15.590
Yes!

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:16.590
France!

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:21.490
In return, Gabon follows French foreign policy
to the word and is its main Uranium supplier.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:25.210
As you know, France is one of the countries
with the most nuclear power plants in the

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.210
world.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:30.330
Well, the uranium they use comes, almost entirely,
from Gabon.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:34.370
And, of course, at a friend's price.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:38.400
Gabon without France is like a car with no
driver.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.889
France without Gabon is like a car with no
fuel

00:05:41.889 --> 00:05:45.210
--Omar Bongo, Gabon president during 42 years.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:49.280
And the same goes for other countries such
as Ivory Coast, whose president was also placed,

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.449
manu militari, by France, in 2011.

00:05:51.449 --> 00:05:54.800
The previous one left the presidential palace
under cannon shots.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.909
And guess who was pulling the trigger!

00:05:56.909 --> 00:05:57.999
Yes, French soldiers.

00:05:57.999 --> 00:06:03.809
In return, Ivory Coast is France’s main
coffee and cocoa supplier.

00:06:03.809 --> 00:06:08.099
, French influence in the region is so complete,
that even the currency they use is controlled

00:06:08.099 --> 00:06:09.099
by France!

00:06:09.099 --> 00:06:14.419
See, the so-called CFA FRANC is the currency
used in 15 of West Africa’s countries, such

00:06:14.419 --> 00:06:17.889
as Mali, Burkina Faso and Ivory Coast...

00:06:17.889 --> 00:06:25.099
Well, it turns out that the Central Bank that
issues this currency is required to keep at

00:06:25.099 --> 00:06:28.250
least half of its foreign currency reserves
in the French Treasury.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:33.150
And, since its creation, the CFA Franc is
linked to French currency: it used to be the

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:34.759
French Franc and now it’s the Euro.

00:06:34.759 --> 00:06:42.369
That means that when the Euro rises or falls,
the CFA Franc simulates its movements.

00:06:42.369 --> 00:06:44.490
But wait a moment because there’s some fine
print!

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.719
And that fine print is the productive economy.

00:06:46.719 --> 00:06:51.089
In other words, France has been running its
former colonies’ policy for decades.

00:06:51.089 --> 00:06:55.419
But these countries have remained just as
poor as when they became independent.

00:06:55.419 --> 00:06:59.399
With the exception of Ivory Coast, the countries
of the African Francophony continue to have

00:06:59.399 --> 00:07:03.449
underdeveloped, agricultural and virtually
stagnant economies.

00:07:03.449 --> 00:07:07.509
No French company has bothered to open factories
in Africa and the money that came from the

00:07:07.509 --> 00:07:11.680
Elysee, was invested in weapons or in extracting
natural resources.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:12.680
Nothing else.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:13.680
After all...

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:14.680
Who wants to do business in Africa?

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:18.830
Well, I think you already know the answer.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:19.830
CHINAFRICA

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:24.789
We’ve told you a thousand times here on
VISUALPOLITIK, today, China is Africa's main

00:07:24.789 --> 00:07:26.289
trading partner.

00:07:26.289 --> 00:07:32.419
Since the 90s, China began to grow economically,
like there was no tomorrow.

00:07:32.419 --> 00:07:35.199
And when one starts growing, one needs resources.

00:07:35.199 --> 00:07:36.469
So far, nothing new.

00:07:36.469 --> 00:07:40.960
But unlike France or any other Western power,
China quickly realized that Africa was more

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.280
than mines and oilfields.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:50.589
I believe Africa is gong to become the next
manufacturing hub of the world and poverty

00:07:50.589 --> 00:07:57.419
will not be a destiny… and many people will
escape poverty.

00:07:57.419 --> 00:08:01.879
Thank you!

00:08:01.879 --> 00:08:05.550
The woman you just heard is Helen Hai and
she’s a Chinese businesswoman.

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:09.379
Her company is called HUAIJIAN and makes shoes
for big brands.

00:08:09.379 --> 00:08:13.789
If you have GUESS or CALVIN KLEIN shoes, it’s
very likely that they were made by this company.

00:08:13.789 --> 00:08:17.319
And I bet you can’t guess where one of their
biggest factories is?

00:08:17.319 --> 00:08:25.430
It’s in Adiss Ababa, Ethiopia’s capital.

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:26.430
Think about it.

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:29.099
In the 90s, China was the Mecca of cheap labor.

00:08:29.099 --> 00:08:33.940
Every large American or European company would
set up its factory in cities such as Shenzhen

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.200
or Guan Zhou.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.920
But as the country grew, salaries grew too.

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:43.360
And by the year 2011, Helen Hai realized that,
if she wanted to cut costs in terms of salaries,

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.380
she needed to find another country.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:47.149
And that country was Ethiopia.

00:08:47.149 --> 00:08:49.760
What’s more, Helen Hai wasn’t traveling
alone.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.709
She had the Chinese government’s support,
which addressed the Ethiopian political elites

00:08:53.709 --> 00:08:59.980
and told them “look, guys, if you let us
do things our way, we can cover the country

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:01.080
with factories, money, and jobs”.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:08.279
And as we usually say around here... so it
was said and done!

00:09:08.279 --> 00:09:15.759
The Hawassa industrial park is already operational
and Ethiopia wants it to become a manufacturing

00:09:15.759 --> 00:09:16.759
hub

00:09:16.759 --> 00:09:18.740
But we're not just talking about Ethiopia!

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.110
There are Chinese factories in many other
countries.

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:25.700
TWYFORD is a company that manufactures ceramic
tiles and its main plant is on the outskirts

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.589
of Nairobi, in Kenya.

00:09:27.589 --> 00:09:31.540
And we can find new industrial parks in other
countries like Ghana.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:36.009
And, even though Chinese companies are supported
by the Government, we’re mostly talking

00:09:36.009 --> 00:09:37.810
about private investment.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.329
And I know what you may be thinking!

00:09:39.329 --> 00:09:45.560
That all of these companies make cheap things
to sell to rich countries, right?

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.350
Well, not at all!

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:52.110
For example, StarTimes is a company in TANZANIA
made with Chinese capital, that provides cable

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.110
TV.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:56.240
Since they reached the market, cable TV prices
have dropped by 90%.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:02.769
Thanks to that, more than 10 million Africans
can enjoy a service that was once a luxury.

00:10:02.769 --> 00:10:05.380
And the same happened with telecommunications.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:08.250
Companies like Huawei have flooded the market
with cheap mobile phones.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:12.250
In fact, nowadays, the same amount of Kenyans
use mobile phones as Europeans.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:17.480
And of course, to connect all these industrial
centers, the Chinese Government has spared

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:18.480
no expense.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:21.230
Do you remember the New Silk Road?

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:24.510
The so-called One Belt, One Road project that
Xi Jimping launched?

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:26.740
Well, the same thing is happening in Africa.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:31.920
And we’re talking about thousands of kilometers
of railroads and roads that have changed the

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:37.649
landscape of several areas of the continent.

00:10:37.649 --> 00:10:45.569
In other words, unlike France, China hasn’t
tried to colonize Africa but has, instead,

00:10:45.569 --> 00:10:47.620
turned them into business partners.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:54.279
And thanks to that, they have managed to earn
more money... and more influence.

00:10:54.279 --> 00:10:59.930
The Confucius Institutes are raising generations
of pro-Chinese Mandarin speakers throughout

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:00.930
Africa

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:02.560
And now you may be wondering.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:03.820
What can France do about this?

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:08.029
Are they just going to sit by while China
engulfs the market?

00:11:08.029 --> 00:11:11.210
We’ll see.

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:12.410
COMMON INTERESTS

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:15.890
I think it won’t surprise you to know that
a large part of African countries aren’t

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:19.970
precisely legal safety paradises that have
a lot of respect for the law.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.850
We’re often talking about dictatorships.

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:27.779
Others are failed states that can barely contain
the fights of various tribes.

00:11:27.779 --> 00:11:31.600
That means that setting up a factory in a
country like Gabon is much more complicated

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:36.050
than in, for example, the United States.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:43.379
It isn’t enough to buy land and get a permit:
you need to have Government contracts.

00:11:43.379 --> 00:11:47.540
That means that, in these cases, diplomacy
plays a fundamental role.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:51.220
Remember how I told you that France controls
its former colonies’ governments with an

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:52.220
iron fist?

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:55.209
Well, you can imagine the rest of the story.

00:11:55.209 --> 00:12:02.420
“French companies must go on the offensive
and fight the growing influence of rival China

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:07.129
for a stake in Africa’s increasingly competitive
markets, France’s Finance Minister Pierre

00:12:07.129 --> 00:12:09.139
Moscovici said on Saturday”

00:12:09.139 --> 00:12:12.850
As you can imagine, if France doesn’t want
China to invest in its former colonies, it

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:14.420
has enough tools to prevent it.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:18.139
And that's why Chinese money has barely reached
these countries.

00:12:18.139 --> 00:12:22.360
Of course Beijing has paid for some projects
in countries like Ivory Coast and Gabon!

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:26.160
But that’s little in comparison to Ethiopia
or Kenya.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.759
However, things could start to change.

00:12:27.759 --> 00:12:32.639
The new French president, Emmanual Macron,
promised to turn the African situation around.

00:12:32.639 --> 00:12:36.529
And it looks like it already started.

00:12:36.529 --> 00:12:40.660
Macron revives France's partnership with China
in Africa

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:44.899
As Macrón said at the press conference, "China
has the money and we have the knowledge of

00:12:44.899 --> 00:12:45.899
the region."

00:12:45.899 --> 00:12:49.949
In other words, France would be willing to
allow the African politicians they control

00:12:49.949 --> 00:12:51.759
to accept Chinese investments.

00:12:51.759 --> 00:12:54.519
In return, they’d require a piece of the
pie.

00:12:54.519 --> 00:12:59.100
Of course, this news is from January 2018,
so there’s still a lot to go through before

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:06.939
we can see how this agreement turns out.

00:13:06.939 --> 00:13:11.259
So now the question is: Do you think France
will change its policy concerning Africa and

00:13:11.259 --> 00:13:14.250
start treating its former colonies as trading
partners?

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.990
Or will they just continue to exchange nice
words?

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:17.990
Do you think that this could be a new push
to bring Africa out of poverty sooner than

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:18.990
expected?

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:19.990
Leave your answer in the comments section.

